<title>PANAMA: PANAMA 96/97 COFFEE CROP SEEN AT 220,137 BAGS.</title>
<headline>PANAMA 96/97 COFFEE CROP SEEN AT 220,137 BAGS.</headline>
<dateline>PANAMA CITY 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Panama's 1996/97 coffee production is forecast at 220,137 60-kg bags, up from 185,418 bags produced during the previous year, the Agriculture Ministry said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Coffee production for the 1997/98 period (Oct 1-Sep 30) is estimated at 218,372 bags, a ministry official said. &quot;The reduction of 2,000 bags is insignificant, this is a normal condition of coffee, it happens all the time,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Because of its lowland geography, Panama grows much less coffee than its Central American neighbors, like Costa Rica or Guatemala.</p>
<p>((--Paul de Bendern, Panama City newsroom, 507 223 7739))</p>
